---
import { DISCORD_INVITE_URL } from '../Header.astro';
import { CONTRIBUTION_REPO_URL, CONTRIBUTION_EMAIL } from '../../lib/site';

export { CONTRIBUTION_REPO_URL, CONTRIBUTION_EMAIL };
---

<div class="contributing">
  <h1 class="contributing__heading">Contributing</h1>
  <p class="contributing__intro">
    This site only works if it stays a community effort: from community to community, not
    from us to you. If you have something to add, fix, or question, we want to hear from you.
  </p>

  <h2 class="contributing__subheading">What kinds of contributions are welcome</h2>
  <ul class="contributing__list">
    <li>Proposing or drafting a new short course or track.</li>
    <li>
      Technical review of existing content: catching something inaccurate, outdated, or
      misleading.
    </li>
    <li>
      Small fixes: typos, broken commands, outdated screenshots, or wording that is unclear.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="contributing__subheading">How to contribute</h2>
  <p>We have a few ways to get involved, in order of preference:</p>
  <ol class="contributing__list">
    <li>
      Open a pull request or issue on our{' '}
      <a href={CONTRIBUTION_REPO_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repo</a>,
      the fastest way for us to review and merge a change.
    </li>
    <li>
      Not comfortable with GitHub? Email your contribution to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTRIBUTION_EMAIL}`}>{CONTRIBUTION_EMAIL}</a> instead, and we will
      take it from there.
    </li>
    <li>
      Not sure where something belongs or how to start? Just ask in the{' '}
      <a href={DISCORD_INVITE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord</a>.
      Someone will be happy to point you in the right direction.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="contributing__subheading">Keep it foundation level</h2>
  <p>
    One thing to keep in mind before you jump in: this project is meant to stay
    foundation-level, free, and plain. We are not trying to upsell anything, and no lesson
    should ever end up reading like a sales pitch. If a contribution starts to feel like
    marketing rather than teaching, it probably needs a rewrite before it fits here. Thanks
    for helping us keep that spirit intact.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .contributing {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .contributing__heading {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.75rem;
  }

  .contributing__subheading {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .contributing__intro,
  .contributing p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .contributing__list {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .contributing__list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .contributing a {
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .contributing {
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem 3rem;
    }

    .contributing__heading {
      font-size: 1.4rem;
    }
  }
</style>
